WEBVTT

01:17.243 --> 01:20.080
THE TRUNK

01:22.082 --> 01:25.043
FIVE MONTHS AGO

01:55.657 --> 01:56.491
What did he…

01:58.326 --> 02:00.203
He said I made him happy.

02:13.508 --> 02:14.884
He's passed.

02:16.719 --> 02:18.138
Ten past three…

02:22.058 --> 02:23.226
Time of death--

02:23.309 --> 02:24.978
No need. I already declared it.

02:28.439 --> 02:30.483
I'm very sorry for your loss.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.902
Please get in touch with his guardian.

02:38.283 --> 02:39.200
Pardon, madam,

02:40.201 --> 02:41.661
but where might you be going?

02:43.746 --> 02:45.582
As of ten minutes ago, I'm divorced.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.768
PROCEED TO YOUR NEXT MARRIAGE?
YES OR NO

04:03.868 --> 04:05.995
I hope your assignment went well, Ms. Noh.

04:15.213 --> 04:17.590
DIVORCE CONFIRMATION

04:17.674 --> 04:20.551
FIELD WIFE TASK COMPLETION REPORT
NOH IN-JI

04:21.970 --> 04:25.181
Deputy Manager Noh, how was your marriage?

04:27.767 --> 04:29.394
Don't you need a vacation?

04:30.353 --> 04:31.771
I'll proceed as usual.

04:33.648 --> 04:34.482
As you wish.

04:42.657 --> 04:44.993
He doesn't exactly match well with you.

04:47.787 --> 04:50.748
It'll be a different type of marriage
from your previous ones.

04:59.924 --> 05:01.718
NM MEMBER PROFILE
HAN JEONG-WON

05:01.801 --> 05:04.804
I heard that prick Han Jeong-won
is making movie music for our company now.

05:05.305 --> 05:07.348
So he's taking a hands-off approach
to management?

05:07.432 --> 05:10.685
- More like his hands were taken off.
- He was blitzed out of his mind earlier.

05:11.644 --> 05:13.187
He's probably off getting high again.

05:13.688 --> 05:14.689
Right?

05:15.189 --> 05:17.108
I fucking knew it. Wait.

05:17.984 --> 05:20.278
Is that why he got divorced? Drugs?

05:20.361 --> 05:22.030
Hell if I know, you prick.

05:22.113 --> 05:23.990
Come on, tell me what's really going on.

05:24.073 --> 05:24.907
I don't know.

05:24.991 --> 05:26.701
You know something. Spill it.

05:26.784 --> 05:27.618
Keep it down.

07:32.994 --> 07:35.872
The person you have called
is currently unavailable…

07:36.456 --> 07:37.957
WIFE

07:38.040 --> 07:39.750
Sleeping pills in the bathroom again?

07:40.543 --> 07:43.963
Why are you stumbling around clubs
like some kind of zombie?

07:44.464 --> 07:46.674
Word on the street
is you're a pill-popper.

07:47.383 --> 07:50.720
Why don't you sleep at home
instead of fucking around in clubs?

07:51.220 --> 07:52.597
I can't sleep at home.

07:53.347 --> 07:54.891
In that huge house of yours?

07:54.974 --> 07:58.478
Try hopping between rooms.
You'll fall asleep in one eventually.

07:58.561 --> 08:01.397
That's what's wrong with you rich folk.
You don't take anything seriously.

08:01.481 --> 08:02.315
Go see a doctor!

08:02.398 --> 08:04.484
I've been going to one for over 20 years.

08:04.984 --> 08:07.487
In fact, I'm about to go to one
for more sleeping pills. Bye.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.045
The person you have called is currently…

08:56.869 --> 08:57.703
WIFE

08:59.872 --> 09:02.583
Please get rid of the lights
in the living room. They're unbearable.

09:03.501 --> 09:06.879
They're not lights, it's an art piece.
A prized possession of your father's.

09:07.672 --> 09:09.131
That's why I hate it so much.

09:10.550 --> 09:12.510
We can't just hang
any random thing up there.

09:13.469 --> 09:15.888
I'm looking for a decent substitute
in France, so just wait.

09:15.972 --> 09:16.806
Don't touch it.

11:33.943 --> 11:34.860
Mr. Han Jeong-won?

11:38.656 --> 11:39.573
It's been a while.

11:47.707 --> 11:50.876
I find that people are more relaxed
when I stand here like this.

11:51.502 --> 11:53.170
You can always refuse, you know.

11:53.254 --> 11:54.088
Then again,

11:54.714 --> 11:57.591
an emergency arrest warrant
would be a bigger headache for you.

11:58.342 --> 11:59.427
Who was it this time?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.637
You know Jay Yoong, right?

12:02.221 --> 12:04.181
Was it Yoong? Wasn't it Young?

12:07.268 --> 12:10.062
Last night at the club, Mr. Jay…

12:10.563 --> 12:12.690
whatever, was arrested on the spot,

12:13.190 --> 12:14.900
and you happened to be there.

12:17.194 --> 12:19.989
Oh my! Thank you.

12:22.324 --> 12:25.035
- Why is it always me?
- You check all the boxes.

12:25.619 --> 12:28.789
You're loaded from selling your shares,
have plenty of free time,

12:28.873 --> 12:30.291
and you have a history.

12:30.916 --> 12:32.877
History? I was just a child.

12:35.337 --> 12:37.339
I'd hardly call a 17-year-old a child.

12:38.007 --> 12:40.718
People that age know right from wrong,
and can choose accordingly.

12:58.903 --> 13:00.988
- Son of a bitch.
- What the--

13:01.071 --> 13:02.782
Jeong-won!

13:02.865 --> 13:04.617
- You bastard!
- What's going on?

13:04.700 --> 13:05.951
- Stop it!
- Let go of me!

13:09.622 --> 13:12.208
- You fucking son of a bitch!
- Mr. Han, sir!

13:12.291 --> 13:15.169
- Mr. Han, please!
- You motherfucker!

13:16.879 --> 13:18.798
I told you, it was that prick!

13:19.298 --> 13:20.508
Why don't you buy me out?

13:20.591 --> 13:23.469
Just run the label.
You own 90%, compared to my tiny 5%.

13:23.552 --> 13:25.930
I like working for you. It's comfy.

13:27.681 --> 13:29.266
I take back calling her a fucking bitch.

13:30.142 --> 13:33.813
I still don't understand
why Lee Seo-yeon dumped you like that.

13:33.896 --> 13:37.525
Seems to me you've stepped in shit.
A pile of shit called Lee Seo-yeon.

13:37.608 --> 13:40.444
So just go over to her
and do whatever it takes to get her back.

13:40.528 --> 13:44.365
Stop tormenting us commoners
and go live your happily ever after!

13:45.366 --> 13:47.660
- I can't.
- What do you mean you can't?

13:47.743 --> 13:49.829
Nothing's impossible
with a bank account like yours.

13:50.704 --> 13:51.914
What would you know?

13:56.919 --> 13:59.880
I'm so grateful you offered
to take care of the remodeling.

14:00.589 --> 14:03.425
I kept telling my husband
we should sell that run-down building,

14:03.509 --> 14:05.344
but he just can't swallow his pride.

14:06.804 --> 14:09.223
I have to ask,
how's life with a younger husband?

14:11.267 --> 14:16.272
He'll never find out you got remarried.
You know me, I'm great at keeping secrets.

14:18.649 --> 14:20.734
HAN JEONG-WON

14:26.657 --> 14:28.325
By the way, is Mr. Han all right?

14:29.535 --> 14:32.037
I heard he got caught
doing drugs at a club--

14:32.538 --> 14:36.584
I mean, there was a misunderstanding,
and he got into a huge fight at the label.

14:44.300 --> 14:46.302
Okay, let's have dinner.

14:47.219 --> 14:48.304
I'll be there by 7:00.

14:50.806 --> 14:53.058
You guys are divorced, right?

14:54.643 --> 14:57.146
I was wondering if you'd remarried
without even getting divorced.

14:59.523 --> 15:01.025
I'm just kidding.

15:02.943 --> 15:05.946
Ms. Yoon-a, do you think you can live
with an empty husk?

15:07.823 --> 15:09.033
I'm also kidding.

15:10.451 --> 15:13.245
Jeong-won's getting married.
That's why we're meeting today.

15:13.329 --> 15:15.039
So don't get any wrong ideas.

15:15.539 --> 15:16.498
He is?

15:18.167 --> 15:19.418
To whom?

15:20.044 --> 15:21.253
Honey!

15:21.754 --> 15:24.089
Han Jeong-won's getting married.
He must be out of his mind!

15:24.173 --> 15:26.550
Maybe seeing Lee Seo-yeon get remarried
made him lose it.

15:26.634 --> 15:28.928
Have you heard anything? Who could it be?

15:29.011 --> 15:32.806
Maybe he met someone at a club.
Is that bastard really on drugs?

15:39.021 --> 15:40.022
Hello.

15:43.984 --> 15:45.986
I take prescription drugs too, you know.

15:47.696 --> 15:48.530
Right.

15:52.993 --> 15:54.411
I'm going now.

15:54.495 --> 15:55.329
Okay.

16:20.729 --> 16:22.523
Your table is over there, ma'am.

16:32.408 --> 16:33.492
It's been a while.

16:34.034 --> 16:35.828
We met at the label just last week.

16:36.870 --> 16:38.205
That's precisely my point.

16:39.331 --> 16:41.458
We're supposed to see each other
every day.

16:42.126 --> 16:43.627
The reason we can't

16:44.420 --> 16:46.714
isn't because of our divorce,
it's because of my remarriage.

16:47.965 --> 16:49.425
Soon you'll be remarried too.

16:55.264 --> 16:57.016
May I take your order?

16:57.099 --> 16:58.475
What's the chef's special?

16:59.643 --> 17:01.228
It's a multi-course meal.

17:01.311 --> 17:03.564
Mini caprese
made with yukhoe and truffle oil,

17:03.647 --> 17:06.775
followed by tomato risotto arancini,
stuffed with cream cheese.

17:06.859 --> 17:08.152
Last, a tenderloin steak,

17:08.235 --> 17:11.697
which comes with a side of prosciutto
and a minced shrimp pesto sauce.

17:11.780 --> 17:14.616
I'd like a cod steak
without tomatoes, please.

17:14.700 --> 17:16.785
One of us here detests tomatoes.

17:17.411 --> 17:19.413
Right, I'll pass that on to the kitchen.

17:30.507 --> 17:32.342
I've had them on me since last week.

17:32.426 --> 17:33.802
I know you like that style.

17:40.059 --> 17:40.893
They're pretty.

17:42.728 --> 17:43.562
Try them on.

17:46.148 --> 17:47.066
Later.

17:49.026 --> 17:51.070
I'm sure you'll enjoy your marriage too.

17:51.153 --> 17:53.238
Why are you doing this to me?

17:53.322 --> 17:54.448
It's only for a year.

17:55.240 --> 17:57.326
Think of it as an arranged marriage.

17:58.160 --> 17:58.994
Seo-yeon.

18:00.370 --> 18:01.663
I can't live without you.

18:02.790 --> 18:06.502
We went to kindergarten together.
I gave up studying abroad to be with you.

18:06.585 --> 18:08.962
You know I can't function without you.

18:09.046 --> 18:11.715
- It would break me.
- You've never tried living without me.

18:14.218 --> 18:15.385
A contract marriage--

18:18.263 --> 18:19.932
A contract marriage, seriously?

18:20.557 --> 18:21.975
You already signed the papers.

18:22.059 --> 18:24.144
You said you'd never see me again
if I didn't.

18:25.979 --> 18:27.689
I know you're trying to punish me,

18:28.315 --> 18:29.525
but you've gone too far.

18:31.110 --> 18:31.944
Me?

18:33.946 --> 18:34.905
I'm punishing you?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.000
I'm the one being punished.

18:47.835 --> 18:50.045
Being alive in front of you
is punishment enough.

18:50.546 --> 18:52.673
If you don't go through
with this marriage,

18:54.174 --> 18:55.008
we're over.

19:07.855 --> 19:09.273
We're done here. I'm heading out.

19:10.149 --> 19:11.525
Let's eat together at home.

19:15.320 --> 19:16.405
My husband's here.

19:17.072 --> 19:18.198
I'm leaving now.

20:38.862 --> 20:40.280
Damn it.

20:59.716 --> 21:02.094
The person you have called is currently…

21:24.783 --> 21:28.328
HAN JEONG-WON

22:02.070 --> 22:06.325
The person you have called
is currently unavailable. Please leave…

22:51.119 --> 22:53.497
You really don't have
a resident registration card on you?

22:54.081 --> 22:55.082
Seriously?

22:55.165 --> 22:56.124
What's this guy in for?

22:58.001 --> 23:00.128
Trying to steal a car.

23:01.338 --> 23:03.340
Caught him red-handed on my way in.

23:05.092 --> 23:08.053
- And the car owner?
- We've been calling but no answer.

23:12.808 --> 23:16.395
Look, mister.
Stonewalling me won't solve anything.

23:16.478 --> 23:17.813
Fancy a night behind bars?

23:35.956 --> 23:36.790
Who are…

23:37.874 --> 23:39.334
I'm Mr. Han Jeong-won's wife.

23:42.462 --> 23:43.296
I see.

23:43.964 --> 23:45.841
So his name's Han Jeong-won, is it?

23:50.971 --> 23:52.764
I've reached the owner of the car.

23:53.765 --> 23:56.726
She says she knew all about it.
She lost her keys and told him to do it.

23:57.227 --> 23:59.271
She knew he was smashing her car window?

23:59.354 --> 24:00.605
May I take him now?

24:02.232 --> 24:03.066
Well…

24:05.068 --> 24:05.902
Let's go, honey.

24:38.810 --> 24:42.063
The owner saw the boat was gone
and hauled it back like that this morning.

24:42.564 --> 24:46.568
Also, a fisherman says he heard a sound
like a gunshot at around one o'clock.

24:47.194 --> 24:49.196
He heard a gunshot but didn't report it?

24:49.863 --> 24:51.490
He thought it was a firecracker.

24:52.365 --> 24:54.534
- Any bullet shells?
- We've yet to find them.

24:55.118 --> 24:56.036
No security cameras?

24:56.536 --> 24:59.247
The one at the kayak house
is the only one in the area,

24:59.831 --> 25:01.166
but someone cut the wires.

25:02.167 --> 25:04.294
So there's no body, just a trunk?

25:05.879 --> 25:09.883
By the way, sir, do you know
how much a trunk like this costs?

25:11.927 --> 25:15.138
50,230,000 won. That's 50 million!

25:18.141 --> 25:20.227
It's a limited-edition piece, apparently.

25:20.310 --> 25:22.103
There are only three
in the entire country.

25:24.231 --> 25:26.566
Call the store,
tell them the serial number,

25:26.650 --> 25:28.026
and find out who bought it.

25:28.109 --> 25:30.529
They keep records of the buyers
for items like these.

25:31.696 --> 25:33.156
How do you even know that?

25:36.660 --> 25:38.995
My wallet's Prada.
You got a problem with that?

25:41.206 --> 25:42.290
It's a knockoff, right, man?

25:43.333 --> 25:44.751
Sir. A knockoff, sir.

25:44.834 --> 25:46.086
All right. Take it.

26:02.894 --> 26:04.354
Would you like me to thank you?

26:04.980 --> 26:07.107
Or should I commend you
for doing your job?

26:08.275 --> 26:09.484
That won't be necessary.

26:10.735 --> 26:13.905
I didn't bring my car
because I was arrested on the spot.

26:13.989 --> 26:15.448
I'll be taking a taxi home.

26:16.908 --> 26:18.368
You can find your own way back.

26:54.654 --> 26:55.739
Get in.

27:01.411 --> 27:02.495
Is this my car?

27:03.079 --> 27:04.039
Yes, so get in.

27:31.191 --> 27:33.735
I think you owe me an explanation.

27:35.779 --> 27:36.863
It was Mr. Kim.

27:38.073 --> 27:39.991
You told him you didn't want a lawyer.

27:45.580 --> 27:46.831
I have a question.

27:48.667 --> 27:49.501
Yes?

27:52.629 --> 27:54.297
You get married for a living.

27:59.969 --> 28:01.346
Do you enjoy this line of work?

28:11.648 --> 28:12.565
It depends.

28:34.546 --> 28:35.422
That one, please.

28:35.922 --> 28:39.843
What great taste.
I'm sure your bride-to-be will love it.

28:40.427 --> 28:43.388
It's my second marriage.
I guess my eye for quality's improved.

28:46.141 --> 28:47.475
- I'll take them.
- Sure.

28:50.812 --> 28:52.981
I see your former wife
recommended us to you.

28:54.607 --> 28:56.317
Isn't that how it is
for all of your clients?

28:58.570 --> 29:00.363
I'm curious,

29:01.030 --> 29:03.241
why does W&L run this kind of business?

29:04.659 --> 29:08.830
Is your wedding business so slow
that you're now matchmaking on the side?

29:13.376 --> 29:17.172
How long do you think
your current marriage will last?

29:18.923 --> 29:21.050
In the future,
as human lifespan increases,

29:21.134 --> 29:23.219
we may end up
having to live with one partner

29:23.303 --> 29:24.137
for 100 years.

29:24.721 --> 29:25.680
100 years.

29:26.890 --> 29:28.057
Could you handle that?

29:30.602 --> 29:33.438
We're in the pursuit
of creating happy marriages.

29:33.938 --> 29:36.065
Trying to stay ahead of the curve,
if you will.

29:39.652 --> 29:42.030
Consider yourself lucky,
Mr. Han Jeong-won.

30:14.938 --> 30:16.356
It's pine nut porridge.

30:16.439 --> 30:18.399
I figured you must have skipped dinner.

30:22.153 --> 30:24.531
I've unpacked in the empty room
on the second floor.

30:24.614 --> 30:27.200
Let me know if you'd like me to move
to a different room.

30:27.283 --> 30:28.743
Do I refer to you as my wife?

30:30.245 --> 30:31.746
Is that how this works?

30:32.914 --> 30:33.748
That's right.

30:36.084 --> 30:37.669
Funny to call you my wife

30:38.711 --> 30:40.213
when everything else is so unofficial.

30:40.922 --> 30:42.841
We offer other types of marriages too.

30:42.924 --> 30:45.385
You specifically chose a discreet one.

30:50.014 --> 30:53.810
It appears I'll need to keep up
this arrangement for the time being.

30:54.561 --> 30:57.146
I'm not sure what I can and can't do.

30:57.230 --> 30:58.648
Then why not check the manual?

31:01.651 --> 31:02.735
Get some sleep.

33:39.892 --> 33:40.810
I get it, okay?

33:43.021 --> 33:44.272
Please stop, Mom.

33:51.320 --> 33:52.238
Mom.

33:54.741 --> 33:55.950
Mom.

34:00.163 --> 34:00.997
Mom.

34:38.701 --> 34:40.828
You're up earlier than I thought.

34:41.496 --> 34:43.164
You don't need to accommodate me.

34:43.664 --> 34:45.333
I usually don't eat at home.

34:45.416 --> 34:48.086
Who said anything about me
catering to your tastes?

34:53.049 --> 34:53.883
Take a seat.

34:55.593 --> 34:57.553
Humor me. It's our first day as newlyweds.

35:14.821 --> 35:18.533
I've been told you like fish.
Apparently, halibut is rich in collagen.

35:19.408 --> 35:20.618
There's something I like

35:21.702 --> 35:23.121
even more than fish.

35:29.127 --> 35:31.045
But I have a weak stomach,

35:31.129 --> 35:32.463
so I'll save it for later.

35:34.215 --> 35:35.550
The smell's a turnoff today.

36:25.266 --> 36:26.475
Let's hear that again.

37:59.026 --> 38:00.444
You're gonna leave that there?

38:01.696 --> 38:02.697
Is that mine?

38:03.239 --> 38:05.199
Well, it's not mine. Bring it in.

38:12.707 --> 38:14.834
I bet it's just another thing
your friend Si-jeong got

38:14.917 --> 38:17.295
instead of actually being paid.

38:25.428 --> 38:26.554
It's not bad.

38:28.139 --> 38:32.059
- Please don't let them die.
- That's not up to me, is it?

38:33.311 --> 38:35.563
You never know
what life's gonna throw at you.

38:36.188 --> 38:38.524
For all we know,
I might die before these guys.

38:39.734 --> 38:41.444
I won't let them starve, though.

38:41.944 --> 38:43.487
And I'll change the water often.

38:49.243 --> 38:51.412
Has the bastard who owns this place
ever been in touch?

38:51.495 --> 38:54.040
All he left behind
is this empty shell of a house.

38:55.249 --> 38:58.085
Please look after the fish
and don't touch anything else.

38:59.879 --> 39:00.963
Did you kill him?

39:05.301 --> 39:07.553
It'd be fine with me if you did.

39:08.471 --> 39:09.805
That would make more sense

39:10.306 --> 39:14.226
than a groom-to-be disappearing for years,
never to be heard from again.

39:15.227 --> 39:16.062
You're right.

39:16.645 --> 39:17.605
I killed him.

39:18.105 --> 39:20.191
You crazy bitch. Just get over him.

39:20.775 --> 39:23.903
Get married, have kids,
and start living like any other bitch.

39:26.822 --> 39:28.657
Keep the coffee machine stocked.

40:00.856 --> 40:03.692
SI-JEONG

40:05.403 --> 40:06.237
Yeah?

40:06.737 --> 40:08.906
Hey, In-ji. That bastard got out.

40:09.490 --> 40:12.493
- Who?
- Who do you think? Eom Tae-seong.

40:13.077 --> 40:15.454
I ran into him
while I was out on a delivery.

40:15.538 --> 40:16.622
How'd the bastard get out?

40:17.706 --> 40:20.167
Wasn't he supposed to rot
in a mental hospital forever?

40:22.336 --> 40:23.295
Where is he now?

40:31.679 --> 40:33.389
God fucking damn it.

40:33.472 --> 40:36.934
Don't do anything for now.
I'll try to find out what happened.

41:36.744 --> 41:38.078
The doors are opening.

41:51.133 --> 41:53.427
I saw the earrings on the back seat.

41:53.511 --> 41:55.262
I know. The police told me.

41:56.931 --> 41:59.642
Thanks for sorting things out
with the police.

42:00.142 --> 42:03.145
Should I… buy you a new car?

42:14.907 --> 42:17.451
I hadn't thrown them away.
I forgot the case after putting them on.

42:20.704 --> 42:22.289
I told you they were pretty, didn't I?

42:25.543 --> 42:27.002
Man, this is so embarrassing.

42:33.926 --> 42:35.219
How was your first night?

42:39.056 --> 42:40.933
All right, I guess.

42:42.560 --> 42:43.394
That's a relief.

42:46.146 --> 42:46.981
Yeah.

42:55.114 --> 42:56.448
The doors are closing.

43:12.715 --> 43:15.968
It'll be over soon.
You're okay when you're with me, remember?

43:19.555 --> 43:21.807
I left my car keys in the office.

43:41.493 --> 43:42.453
I guess this…

43:45.289 --> 43:47.416
is like separation anxiety dogs must feel.

43:49.293 --> 43:50.628
I'll be better.

43:51.795 --> 43:53.005
Come back. We'll start over.

43:53.088 --> 43:56.342
This whole arrangement is ridiculous,
you know.

43:57.760 --> 43:58.594
Honey.

43:59.762 --> 44:00.596
I wish…

44:02.640 --> 44:05.309
you would die.

44:08.562 --> 44:10.022
The doors are opening.

44:14.568 --> 44:16.070
The doors are closing.

44:57.986 --> 44:58.821
Hello?

44:59.613 --> 45:01.782
Come on out. Don't just stay in there.

45:14.294 --> 45:15.337
Are you a good cook?

45:17.214 --> 45:18.048
Sometimes.

45:27.349 --> 45:29.476
Don't overthink it.

45:29.560 --> 45:31.520
"Happily ever after,
'til death do us part."

45:31.603 --> 45:33.355
That only applies to us for a year.

45:42.781 --> 45:43.949
This isn't bad.

45:44.658 --> 45:45.993
The fish did all the work.

45:46.827 --> 45:48.871
They were expensive. I used your card.

46:00.632 --> 46:01.842
Is this whole thing

46:02.968 --> 46:05.637
like an expensive
live-in housemaid service?

46:09.641 --> 46:10.684
Is sex included?

46:14.605 --> 46:17.775
Or would you be fine with a husband
who cheats on you every day?

46:19.026 --> 46:20.235
I love women, you know.

46:22.654 --> 46:23.989
Is that what you want?

47:28.887 --> 47:30.264
Is it not allowed?

47:34.268 --> 47:35.435
We're married, aren't we?

47:43.819 --> 47:44.653
It's allowed.

47:50.450 --> 47:51.410
If we both want it.

48:01.545 --> 48:03.130
It'll be a while then, I guess.

48:06.592 --> 48:08.343
I'm rather shy, you see.

48:18.645 --> 48:20.105
Thanks for the meal, or…

48:22.274 --> 48:24.318
maybe a thanks is unnecessary.

48:24.902 --> 48:26.403
I haven't read the manual yet.

50:20.851 --> 50:22.185
What do you think you're…

50:23.729 --> 50:26.481
I'm sorry if I woke you up.
I just really have to watch this match.

50:27.566 --> 50:28.734
Do you like soccer?

50:29.443 --> 50:30.277
No.

50:30.360 --> 50:31.361
Baseball?

50:32.446 --> 50:34.031
I detest chasing after balls.

50:34.781 --> 50:36.950
I knew you wouldn't be a fan
of team sports.

50:38.535 --> 50:40.370
Buy a TV for your room.
Buy as many as you want.

50:45.333 --> 50:46.793
Does it bother you that much?

50:46.877 --> 50:49.504
I guess your so-called system
isn't all it's cracked up to be.

50:50.005 --> 50:53.383
I'm an insomniac on too many pills.
How did you miss this?

50:53.967 --> 50:55.052
I saw your file.

50:56.303 --> 50:58.805
I know you can't sleep
or do much of anything without drugs.

50:59.306 --> 51:01.183
You're not sleeping anytime soon,
so join me.

51:01.266 --> 51:02.476
Hey!

51:02.559 --> 51:05.187
Maybe you'll fall asleep
if you watch something boring.

51:06.313 --> 51:07.147
Ms. Noh In-ji.

51:07.230 --> 51:08.065
Honey.

51:11.026 --> 51:11.860
Want a beer?

51:12.778 --> 51:13.987
There's some downstairs.

51:15.489 --> 51:16.323
Wait right here.

52:01.952 --> 52:05.413
It seems what you lack in mental fortitude
you make up for in agility.

52:05.914 --> 52:07.916
I'm fine with you living somewhere else.

52:09.334 --> 52:12.963
If you need a place, just say so.
I won't tell your company.

52:13.839 --> 52:14.673
All I want

52:16.341 --> 52:18.468
is for the next year
to pass by quietly, so--

52:18.552 --> 52:19.469
Mr. Han Jeong-won.

52:26.184 --> 52:27.811
Do you like playing hard to get?

52:29.896 --> 52:31.815
I'm not trying to seduce you.

52:33.859 --> 52:36.194
So you can relax around me.

52:39.906 --> 52:42.325
It's okay to just be yourself,

52:43.660 --> 52:45.120
at least when you're with me.

55:05.885 --> 55:09.264
How do you know the owner of the trunk?

55:12.642 --> 55:13.601
I'm her husband.

57:28.153 --> 57:31.489
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
